    "turns": [
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "Why does AlphaTensor deserve its own place in the history of artificial intelligence?",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial-hook"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "Matrix multiplication is a basic operation behind scientific computing and machine learning, yet finding algorithms with fewer scalar multiplications is a difficult combinatorial problem. Before AlphaTensor, major improvements were usually derived through sustained human mathematical work.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-alphatensor-deepmind", "source-primary-record"],
            "claimIds": [
                "claim-annual-membership",
                "claim-publication-record",
                "claim-contributor-record",
                "claim-core-method",
                "claim-historical-significance"
            ],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.historical-background"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "AlphaTensor encodes the multiplication tensor as a game state, where each move subtracts a rank-one tensor until the target is reduced to zero. A neural network and tree search learn to choose moves that produce short, valid decompositions.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-alphatensor-deepmind", "source-primary-record"],
            "claimIds": [
                "claim-annual-membership",
                "claim-publication-record",
                "claim-contributor-record",
                "claim-core-method",
                "claim-historical-significance"
            ],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.core-idea"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "Experts generally treat AlphaTensor as a landmark for AI-assisted algorithm discovery because the output is an explicit, verifiable algorithm. It broadened the AlphaZero paradigm from board games to mathematical search and inspired later work on optimizing low-level computation.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-alphatensor-deepmind", "source-primary-record"],
            "claimIds": [
                "claim-annual-membership",
                "claim-publication-record",
                "claim-contributor-record",
                "claim-core-method",
                "claim-historical-significance"
            ],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.long-term-legacy"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "As today's systems grow larger, which lessons from AlphaTensor still matter, and which limits deserve to be questioned again?",
